# Anti AI-template UI

Soft skills alone failed. Visual tropes are gated by `npm run anti-ai-ui` (`scripts/check-anti-ai-ui.mjs`) and this rule.

## Before any UI / CSS / landing work

1. Read `.agents/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` and `.agents/skills/make-interfaces-feel-better/SKILL.md`.
2. For marketing / landing / promotional surfaces, also read `.agents/skills/landing-page-design/SKILL.md`.
3. Pick **one named direction** (e.g. daylight print, industrial utility, editorial magazine). Write it in the PR or commit body. Do not ship an unnamed “nice dark UI”.

## Forbidden as a first default

- Font stacks led by Inter, Roboto, Open Sans, Arial, Helvetica Neue, or generic `system-ui` / `-apple-system` as the primary face.
- Purple / indigo AI tokens and purple-to-indigo gradient tropes (see script header bans).
- Three equal marketing cards in a row as the hero composition.
- Cream paper + terracotta accent + display serif cliché.
- **Nightglass:** dark field + film-grain / noise overlay + neon mint or cyan as the default “AI tool” night mode.

Prefer daylight, print, or utility looks when unsure. Neon accents and grain are not a substitute for a direction.

## Proof

- Feature Map **Looks** section: read a control-glass screenshot; confirm brand-first composition and no banned tropes.
- CI: `npm run anti-ai-ui` must stay green. Second smell of the same trope → extend the script, not another soft reminder.
